  "n_s13" [label="(13,0,0) Currently, CuI has been used to stabilize/constrain phosphorus nanorods and anionic P12^2−/P14^2− species as adducts."];
  "n_s15" [label="(15,0,0) Currently, because these host-derived phosphorus materials are amorphous, their structural determination remains elusive."];
  "n_s16" [label="(16,0,0) Currently, MOFs (host–guest chemistry, tuneable porosity, crystallinity, stability) are ideal hosts to include P4, potentially polymerize it with visible light, and analyze products by diffraction."];
  "n_s17" [label="(17,0,0) Currently, doping MOFs with atomic-width phosphorus chains may improve semiconducting properties of P–MOF composites."];
  "n_s18" [label="(18,0,0) Currently, a double-helical phosphorus chain of butterfly P8 monomers can be synthesized and stabilized within helical channels of indium-based MOF MFM-300(In)."];
